---
// Guide page: camping at WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca, written for people
// deciding where to sleep for a race weekend — the INDYCAR season finale on
// 4-6 September 2026 in particular.
//
// NOT an event page. It deliberately emits no Event JSON-LD: it describes a
// facility and a set of policies, not a scheduled occurrence, and marking it up
// as an Event to win a rich result would be misusing the vocabulary. It shares
// no copy with the event templates.
//
// SOURCING: every fact here comes from weathertechraceway.com and is linked
// inline at the point it is used. Where the raceway publishes nothing — camping
// prices, the General Parking charge, quiet hours, generator rules — the page
// says so and names who to ask. Those absences are findings, not gaps: several
// of them are the reason this page is worth reading.
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const site = "https://montereybayevents.com";
const title = "Laguna Seca Camping — Areas, Access & What Is Not Published";
const description =
  "Every camping area at WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca, which gate serves it, the 40-foot RV limit and six-adult cap — plus the prices the raceway does not publish.";
const canonical = `${site}/laguna-seca/camping/`;

const CAMPING = "https://weathertechraceway.com/pages/camping";
const TICKETS = "https://weathertechraceway.com/pages/ticket-information";
const INDYCAR = "https://weathertechraceway.com/pages/indycar-grand-prix-of-monterey";
const PHONE = "(831) 242-8200";

const premier = [
  "Chaparral",
  "Can-Am",
  "Corkscrew View",
  'Lower Terrace "E-5"',
  'Turn 5 Right "T5R"',
];
const reserved = [
  "Grand Prix",
  "Corkscrew Upper View",
  'Upper Terrace "E-6"',
  'Terrace "E-7"',
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description.slice(0, 155)} />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon" />

    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description.slice(0, 200)} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Monterey Bay Events" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`${site}/og-default.jpg`} />

    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description.slice(0, 200)} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={`${site}/og-default.jpg`} />
    {/* No structured data. This is a guide to a facility, not an event —
        see the note at the top of this file. */}
  </Fragment>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <a
      href="/events/september/"
      class="text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground hover:text-brass"
    >
      ← Central Coast events in September 2026
    </a>

    <h1 class="mt-6 text-5xl leading-[0.9] sm:text-6xl">
      Camping at <span class="text-brass">Laguna Seca</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-7 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
      WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca has ten named camping areas in three
      tiers, a hard 40-foot limit on RVs and a six-adult cap per site. Every
      camper needs an event admission ticket as well as a camping pass. What it
      costs is the part you cannot look up: the raceway publishes no camping
      rates online at all, and no price for General Parking either, while
      selling Preferred and season parking passes. Budget for a charge you
      cannot check in advance, and call
      <a href={`tel:+18312428200`} class="text-brass hover:underline">{PHONE}</a>
      before you plan a weekend around a number.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="border-b border-border/70 pb-2 text-3xl text-brass">
        The three tiers, and the ten areas
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        The raceway groups camping into Premier, Reserved and General, and the
        difference is hook-ups and how you book rather than only position.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-foreground">Premier — {premier.length} areas</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        {premier.join(" · ")}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        These carry <em>“partial hook-ups and/or an excellent view of the
        track”</em>. Note the “and/or” — the raceway does not say which of the
        five have hook-ups and which are there for the view, so if you need
        power, confirm the specific area before booking rather than assuming
        Premier means serviced.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-foreground">Reserved — {reserved.length} areas</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        {reserved.join(" · ")}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        These may include a fire pit and a picnic table, with hillside or track
        views. “May” is the raceway’s word, and it is doing work: it is not a
        guarantee for any given site.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-foreground">General — outside Turns 9, 10 and 11</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Dry camping. No hook-ups, no picnic tables, no barbecue pits. The
        raceway’s wording is worth reading precisely: <em>“You are guaranteed
        space, however there are not designated areas.”</em> You will get in;
        you will not get a numbered pitch. Arrive early if you want to choose
        where you sit.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Source:{" "}
        <a href={CAMPING} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          Camping and Recreation, WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="border-b border-border/70 pb-2 text-3xl text-brass">
        Rules that decide whether you can come at all
      </h2>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3">
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="text-brass">—</span>
          <span><strong class="text-foreground">RVs: maximum length 40 feet.</strong> A hard limit, not a guideline. Measure before you book a coach.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="text-brass">—</span>
          <span><strong class="text-foreground">Six adults per site</strong>, with children under 15 not counted against it.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="text-brass">—</span>
          <span><strong class="text-foreground">Every camper needs an admission ticket</strong> for the duration of the event, children under 15 excepted. A camping pass alone does not get you in.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="text-brass">—</span>
          <span><strong class="text-foreground">Check-in 2:00–5:00 p.m. daily, check-out 12 noon.</strong> The check-in window is three hours; arriving at seven in the evening is not covered by it.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="text-brass">—</span>
          <span><strong class="text-foreground">Two pets per site</strong>, fees apply and rabies verification is required — though pet camping fees are waived during premier events.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="text-brass">—</span>
          <span><strong class="text-foreground">No overnight parking</strong> in the General or Preferred parking areas. Sleeping at the track requires a camping pass, not a parking pass.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Sources:{" "}
        <a href={CAMPING} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-brass hover:underline">Camping and Recreation</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href={TICKETS} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-brass hover:underline">Ticket Information</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="border-b border-border/70 pb-2 text-3xl text-brass">
        Getting in: South Boundary Road, not Highway 68
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        This is the single thing most likely to cost you an hour. For the 2026
        season the raceway is explicit:{" "}
        <em>“When entering the park during any of our Major 2026 Season events,
        you must come in through the South Boundary Rd. entrance to the park.”</em>
        {" "}The INDYCAR finale is one of those events. Do not route to the
        Highway 68 main entrance out of habit or because a map app sends you
        there.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        General Parking is the Purple 10 area, also reached from South Boundary
        Road. Preferred Parking is the Green Lakebed area. Will-call runs from
        7 a.m. until halfway through the last race of the day, again via South
        Boundary Road.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Gates “generally open at 7 a.m. during race events” and close at 10 p.m.
        or midnight depending on the event — the raceway’s own hedge, not ours.
        No gate times specific to 4–6 September have been published.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Source:{" "}
        <a href={TICKETS} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          Ticket Information, WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="border-b border-border/70 pb-2 text-3xl text-brass">
        The INDYCAR weekend, 4–6 September 2026
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        The Grand Prix of Monterey closes the NTT INDYCAR Series and INDY NXT
        seasons — the champion is crowned here, which is the kind of weekend
        that fills a campground. General tent camping is available across
        3–7 September, so you can be on site the day before running starts and
        stay the night after the race.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Premium trackside camping is sold separately alongside the Turn 3 VIP
        Club, new for 2026. The Champions Club is already sold out.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        For the full on-track schedule, ticket tiers and what a general
        admission ticket includes, see our{" "}
        <a href="/event/indycar-grand-prix-of-monterey/" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          INDYCAR Grand Prix of Monterey guide
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Source:{" "}
        <a href={INDYCAR} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          INDYCAR Grand Prix of Monterey, WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="border-b border-border/70 pb-2 text-3xl text-brass">
        How to book, and why you may have to phone
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        General camping can be booked online, and walk-ins are taken at the
        Entry Station until 5:00 p.m. daily. Premier and Reserved sites are
        different: during premier events — which the INDYCAR finale is — they
        are <strong class="text-foreground">reservable by phone only</strong>, on{" "}
        <a href={`tel:+18312428200`} class="text-brass hover:underline">{PHONE}</a>.
        The office runs weekdays, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m., or{" "}
        <a href="mailto:tickets@laguna-seca.com" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          tickets@laguna-seca.com
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        That matters for planning. If you want a hook-up or a track view for
        race weekend, you cannot do it at midnight from a laptop — you have to
        reach a person during California business hours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-l-2 border-brass bg-surface/60 px-6 py-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl text-brass">What nobody publishes</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        These are not gaps in our research. We looked, and the raceway does not
        put them online.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4">
        <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <strong class="text-foreground">Camping rates, for any tier.</strong>{" "}
          No nightly rate, no weekend rate, no indication of whether camping is
          sold per night or as an event pass. The camping page points to Event
          Camping Guide PDFs and the ticket office. Ask on {PHONE}.
        </li>
        <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <strong class="text-foreground">The General Parking price.</strong>{" "}
          The raceway publishes exactly where General Parking is — the Purple 10
          area, off South Boundary Road — but not what it costs, while
          separately selling Preferred Parking and season parking passes. The
          asymmetry is deliberate enough to be worth stating: budget for a
          parking charge on arrival and confirm the amount with the ticket
          office rather than assuming it is free because no price appears.
        </li>
        <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <strong class="text-foreground">Quiet hours and generator rules.</strong>{" "}
          Neither appears on the camping page. For a campground where dry
          sites and RVs share ground outside Turns 9 to 11, that is the
          question most likely to affect whether you sleep.
        </li>
        <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <strong class="text-foreground">When camping sells out for the
          INDYCAR weekend.</strong> No sell-out date, no remaining-capacity
          indicator, and no waitlist is published for camping. The Champions
          Club is marked sold out; camping is not marked either way.
        </li>
        <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <strong class="text-foreground">Whether Watkins Gate opens for this
          event.</strong> Older Laguna Seca event material describes a Watkins
          Gate entrance restricted to Saturdays. It does not appear on the
          raceway’s current ticket information, which names only South Boundary
          Road for 2026 major events. Treat South Boundary Road as the entrance
          and ask the ticket office if you specifically need another.
        </li>
        <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <strong class="text-foreground">Off-site alternatives.</strong> The
          raceway publishes none, and we are not going to invent drive times
          from campgrounds it does not endorse. If on-site camping is full, the
          ticket office is the right first call — they know what the overflow
          arrangement is for a given weekend and we do not.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-border/70 pt-8">
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Driving in for the weekend rather than camping? The{" "}
        <a href="/traffic/" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          traffic, closures and parking guide
        </a>{" "}
        covers road conditions across the Peninsula, including the Highway 1
        closure through Big Sur that is still in force. Everything else on the
        September calendar is on the{" "}
        <a href="/events/september/" class="text-brass hover:underline">
          September 2026 events page
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
